# NUC-45: per-job override for agent_propose.sh (AGENT_JOB_OVERRIDES) — morning job.
# Non-secret task wiring only; API keys stay in the canonical secrets.env, sourced first.
#
# EXAMPLE ONLY. The live file lives OUTSIDE git at
#   ~/.config/agent-workforce/daily_plan.env  (mode 600, owned by dave)
# and is intentionally NOT committed — mirrors m1_signal_scan.env exactly.
# Install: copy the vars below into that path, then chmod 600.
#
# Runtime is headless Claude Code on the box subscription ($0 OpenRouter spend, which
# stays paused). agent_propose.sh is runtime-agnostic — it just execs AGENT_RUNTIME_CMD.
AGENT_PROFILE=claude-sonnet
AGENT_TASK_SLUG=daily-plan
# ops mode (NUC-36): lock / preflight / cost / scorecard only. No inbox worktree, no
# write-boundary, no proposal commit — this job's artifact is a Notion row.
AGENT_RUN_MODE=ops
AGENT_MAX_ATTEMPTS=2
AGENT_TIMEOUT_MINUTES=15
AGENT_RUNTIME_CMD='~/agent-workforce/bin/run_daily_plan_cc.sh'
# LOAD-BEARING (2026-07-21 regression): the runtime exits 0 when a provider error becomes
# the agent's final response, so exit code alone is not evidence anything was written.
# notion_daily.py drops a receipt only after Notion accepts the upsert, and -newermt ties
# the assertion to THIS run — yesterday's receipt cannot satisfy today's check.
AGENT_VERIFY_CMD='find "$HOME/logs/daily-plan" -name "receipt-*.json" -newermt "@$AGENT_RUN_STARTED_AT" | grep -q .'
